    {
      "id": "scene_P0lFCIBJ_n",
      "type": "quiz",
      "order": 4,
      "title": "Quiz 1 – CSS Basics",
      "actions": [
        {
          "id": "action_LTiZt6GL",
          "text": "Good morning, everyone! Let’s dive into a quick quiz to see how well we’ve grasped the basics of CSS selectors. Read each question carefully, and remember: a selector is the part of a CSS rule that tells the browser which HTML elements to style.",
          "type": "speech"
        },
        {
          "id": "action_xzU4DZ-B",
          "text": "For the first question, look at the rule `h1.title { color: blue; font-size: 24px; }`. The selector is the pattern before the opening brace—here it’s `h1.title`. The properties inside the braces (`color` and `font-size`) tell the browser *what* to change, but they aren’t part of the selector.",
          "type": "speech"
        },
        {
          "id": "action_MNo2y2vH",
          "text": "The second question asks you to pick all selectors that would match `<p class=\"intro\" id=\"first\">Welcome</p>`. Think about how selectors target elements: a tag name (`p`), a class (`.intro`), and an ID (`#first`). Combining them is allowed, as long as you use the correct syntax. So `p.intro`, `#first`, and `p#first.intro` are all valid ways to select that paragraph.",
          "type": "speech"
        },
        {
          "id": "action_jbG3yEIr",
          "type": "discussion",
          "topic": "Why is it important to choose the most specific selector you need, and how does selector specificity affect which styles are applied?",
          "prompt": "Share any examples where a too‑general selector caused unexpected styling, or where a specific selector helped you fix a bug.",
          "agentId": "default-4"
        }
      ],
      "content": {
        "type": "quiz",
        "questions": [
          {
            "id": "q1",
            "type": "single",
            "answer": [
              "A"
            ],
            "points": 5,
            "options": [
              {
                "value": "A",
                "label": "h1.title"
              },
              {
                "value": "B",
                "label": "color: blue;"
              },
              {
                "value": "C",
                "label": "font-size: 24px;"
              },
              {
                "value": "D",
                "label": "The curly braces {}"
              }
            ],
            "analysis": "The selector is the part before the opening curly brace that tells the browser which HTML elements to style. In this rule, 'h1.title' selects any <h1> element with class 'title'. The other parts are declarations or punctuation.",
            "question": "Which part of the following CSS rule is the selector?\n```css\nh1.title { color: blue; font-size: 24px; }\n```",
            "hasAnswer": true
          },
          {
            "id": "q2",
            "type": "multiple",
            "answer": [
              "A",
              "B",
              "D"
            ],
            "points": 8,
            "options": [
              {
                "value": "A",
                "label": "p.intro"
              },
              {
                "value": "B",
                "label": "#first"
              },
              {
                "value": "C",
                "label": ".welcome"
              },
              {
                "value": "D",
                "label": "p#first.intro"
              }
            ],
            "analysis": "The element can be selected by its tag and class (p.intro), by its id (#first), or by combining tag, id, and class (p#first.intro). The selector '.welcome' looks for a class named 'welcome', which this element does not have, so it is incorrect.",
            "question": "Select all selectors that would correctly apply a style to the following HTML element:\n```html\n<p class=\"intro\" id=\"first\">Welcome</p>\n```",
            "hasAnswer": true
          }
        ]
      },
      "stageId": "m22Ov_nWB7",
      "createdAt": 1777903130360,
      "updatedAt": 1777903130360
